<h2>Math</h2>

<p>
  Inline math sits in the text: Euler's identity is <tex>e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0</tex>, and a $5 price stays a price.
  Display math goes between double dollars and follows the slide's alignment:
</p>

<tex>\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}
\qquad
\sum_{k=1}^{n} k = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}</tex>

<p>Math reveals like any other item: put it in a <c><step></c>.</p>

<notes>
  KaTeX renders math to plain HTML (no scripts at runtime), so it works in every build target and in the PDF.
</notes>
